TASK-247 runtime harness: notifications.onClicked / onClosed reach the API
Explorer's worker in the running app. Temporary code, never committed to
Detour/. Apply, build, run, revert:

    git apply docs/harness/task247-harness.patch
    xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    OUT="<scratch dir>"; mkdir -p "$OUT"
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify247 DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR="$OUT" DETOUR_REPO="$PWD" \
        .derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour -ExtensionConsoleLogPublic YES &
    # wait for "done" in $OUT/verify.log (about 65 s), then kill that pid
    git apply -R docs/harness/task247-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    # delete the -DetourVerify247 autosave keys from com.detourbrowser.mac and
    # ~/Library/Application Support/DetourVerify247

Installs a fake notification center as `shared` (the Debug build's permission
is not asked for and the user's Notification Center is never touched), installs
TestExtensions/api-explorer, waits for its worker to park, creates three
notifications through the manager, then calls handleResponse with their
delivered identifiers (click, dismiss) and clears the third. It logs the
owner's event channel after each step, idles 50 s so WebKit unloads the
worker, and clicks again: a new incarnation must take the event. The worker's
"[API Explorer] notifications.onClicked/onClosed" lines are in the unified log
(category extension-polyfill).

